%I A401995 #6 Nov 16 2026 21:52:06
%S A401995 2,10,94,2176,124038,16090454,4381024074,2414625930820,
%T A401995 2666547526089128,5891426963604086524,26042289902662772592650,
%U A401995 230315819459834896791707952,4074850113444639818722930320980,144211348254400566590826233479940306
%N A401995 Number of digraphs on n unlabeled nodes, self-loops allowed, that are reducible for some election of source-SCC headers.
%C A401995 An election chooses one node in each source strongly connected component and adds a new root with edges to those chosen nodes. At least one such election must yield a reducible flow graph.
%C A401995 Self-loops never affect reducibility (transformation T1 deletes them), so the labeled loopy count is 2^n times the simple one; the unlabeled counts are genuinely distinct (Burnside classes gain a factor 2^(number of cycles) for the fixed loop sets).
%D A401995 F. Harary and E. M. Palmer, Graphical Enumeration, Academic Press, NY, 1973.
%D A401995 M. S. Hecht and J. D. Ullman, Flow graph reducibility, SIAM J. Comput. 1 (1972), 188-202.
%D A401995 M. S. Hecht and J. D. Ullman, Characterizations of reducible flow graphs, J. ACM 21 (1974), 367-375.
%D A401995 R. W. Robinson, Counting digraphs with restrictions on the strong components, in T.-H. Ku (ed.), Combinatorics and Graph Theory '95, World Scientific, Singapore, 1995, pp. 343-354.
%D A401995 R. E. Tarjan, Testing flow graph reducibility, J. Comput. System Sci. 9 (1974), 355-365.
%H A401995 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A401995/b401995.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..19</a>
%H A401995 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A397968/a397968.py.txt">Required Python module (unlabeled_reducible_cfgs.py)</a>, Aug 2026.
%H A401995 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A400123/a400123_1.py.txt">Required Python module (everywhere_reducible.py)</a>, Sep 2026.
%H A401995 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A398465/a398465.py.txt">Required Python module (labeled_reducible_cfgs.py)</a>, Jul 2026.
%H A401995 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A401321/a401321_1.py.txt">Required Python module (valid_header_elections.py)</a>, Oct 2026.
%H A401995 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A399885/a399885.py.txt">Python program (unlabeled_reducible_elections.py)</a>, Nov 2026.
%F A401995 a(n) = (1/n!) * Sum_{sigma in S_n} 2^c(sigma) * F_some(sigma), where c(sigma) is the number of cycles of sigma and F_some(sigma) counts loopless digraphs fixed by sigma that admit at least one reducible election of source-SCC headers.
%o A401995 (Python)
%o A401995 # Save the five linked Python files in one directory using the filenames
%o A401995 # shown in their link captions, then run Python in that directory.
%o A401995 from unlabeled_reducible_elections import unlabeled_election_sequence
%o A401995 unlabeled_election_sequence("unlabeled_reducible_digraphs_some_loops", 16)
%Y A401995 Cf. A000595 (all unlabeled loopy digraphs).
%K A401995 nonn,new
